{"kind":"symbol","sections":[],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Origami’s patch graph and SwiftUI are both reactive dataflow. Swami targets SwiftUI’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"state graph (computed properties, "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"@State"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"withAnimation"},{"type":"text","text":") rather than imperative"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"functions, so the two graphs stay aligned. Where a native SwiftUI construct maps"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"cleanly, Swami uses it. Where Origami’s semantics need a helper — for example the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"Interaction patch’s four discrete output ports, or Drag’s momentum + rubber-band"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"physics — Swami ships a helper named after the Origami patch and shaped like it."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Corpus-in-progress-2-of-69","type":"heading","level":2,"text":"Corpus (in progress — 2 of 69)"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The translated corpus is the gallery and the training set. Each entry is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"verified SwiftUI translation of an Origami pattern."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Interaction","type":"heading","level":3,"text":"Interaction"},{"items":[{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"doc:Interaction_Touch"}]}]},{"content":[{"type":"paragraph","inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami\/Interaction_Drag"}]}]}],"type":"unorderedList"}],"kind":"content"}],"identifier":{"url":"doc:\/\/samatwork.Swami\/documentation\/Swami","interfaceLanguage":"swift"},"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"major":0,"minor":3},"variants":[{"tr